{"id":"evt_0e1d5dfc1001QyXsmtxHphrzfc","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_w4mg9vpzso8a_1","state":{"metadata":{"output":"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\n"},"status":"running","input":{"command":"echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.log 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.port===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.port 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\" && head -15 /tmp/pr24.md 2>/dev/null"},"time":{"start":1790495285162}},"id":"prt_0e1d5de33001b8jJOeaQv6zSDr","sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","messageID":"msg_0e1d5cfea001rxUdU3ICS59WmO"},"time":1790495285185}}
{"id":"evt_0e1d5dfc6001tabz4Og0sL2vRM","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_w4mg9vpzso8a_1","state":{"metadata":{"output":"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\nopencode server listening on http://127.0.0.1:4096\n===/tmp/ocspike.port===\n4096\n===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\nMain already has a self-update from #25. This PR keeps what #25 did well and swaps in the stronger parts of this branch.\n\n## What changes compared to main\n\n- **Pure Go install.** `drawa --update` and the page now download the release asset, check it against `checksums.txt`, and swap the binary in atomically (staged next to it, then `rename`). Before, they ran `install.sh` from `main`, so an update depended on whatever `main` held at that moment. It no longer needs `sh`, `curl` or `tar`, and downloads time out after 5 minutes.\n- **Numeric version comparison.** Tags are compared number by number, so `v0.10.0` counts as newer than `v0.9.0`. Covered by tests, along with reading the release tag from the `releases/latest` redirect.\n- **A small update dialog instead of the bottom notice.** It shows `v0.1.6 \u2192 v0.1.7` with a *What's new* link, *Not now*, *Update*, and *Skip this version* as a quiet text link. The app behind it is only lightly dimmed.\n  - *Not now* asks again in a day, and *Skip this version* waits for the next release. It also checks when you return to the tab, so it can't pop up every time you switch back.\n  - **Update installs now, and the restart is your choice.** After installing, the dialog asks *Restart now* or *Restart later*. That's also where it warns that restarting stops sessions that are still working. With *Restart later*, the new version starts the next time you run drawa, and the server remembers the install so the dialog doesn't offer that version again.\n  - Progress and errors show inside the dialog. An error offers *Try again* and points to `drawa --update`.\n  - After *Restart now*, the page reloads once the server answers as the new version.\n- `#confirm`'s styles are now a shared `.prompt` class, used by both dialogs.\n\nThe endpoints are `GET /api/version`, `POST /api/update` (install only) and `POST /api/update/restart`, which refuses when nothing is installed. That way, a page already open on v0.1.7 still reloads after updating to a build with this change.\n\n"},"status":"running","input":{"command":"echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.log 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.port===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.port 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\" && head -15 /tmp/pr24.md 2>/dev/null"},"time":{"start":1790495285162}},"id":"prt_0e1d5de33001b8jJOeaQv6zSDr","sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","messageID":"msg_0e1d5cfea001rxUdU3ICS59WmO"},"time":1790495285190}}
{"id":"evt_0e1d5dfcd001yIF1LOX4Jyo2cJ","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_function_w4mg9vpzso8a_1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.log 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.port===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.port 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\" && head -15 /tmp/pr24.md 2>/dev/null"},"output":"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\nopencode server listening on http://127.0.0.1:4096\n===/tmp/ocspike.port===\n4096\n===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\nMain already has a self-update from #25. This PR keeps what #25 did well and swaps in the stronger parts of this branch.\n\n## What changes compared to main\n\n- **Pure Go install.** `drawa --update` and the page now download the release asset, check it against `checksums.txt`, and swap the binary in atomically (staged next to it, then `rename`). Before, they ran `install.sh` from `main`, so an update depended on whatever `main` held at that moment. It no longer needs `sh`, `curl` or `tar`, and downloads time out after 5 minutes.\n- **Numeric version comparison.** Tags are compared number by number, so `v0.10.0` counts as newer than `v0.9.0`. Covered by tests, along with reading the release tag from the `releases/latest` redirect.\n- **A small update dialog instead of the bottom notice.** It shows `v0.1.6 \u2192 v0.1.7` with a *What's new* link, *Not now*, *Update*, and *Skip this version* as a quiet text link. The app behind it is only lightly dimmed.\n  - *Not now* asks again in a day, and *Skip this version* waits for the next release. It also checks when you return to the tab, so it can't pop up every time you switch back.\n  - **Update installs now, and the restart is your choice.** After installing, the dialog asks *Restart now* or *Restart later*. That's also where it warns that restarting stops sessions that are still working. With *Restart later*, the new version starts the next time you run drawa, and the server remembers the install so the dialog doesn't offer that version again.\n  - Progress and errors show inside the dialog. An error offers *Try again* and points to `drawa --update`.\n  - After *Restart now*, the page reloads once the server answers as the new version.\n- `#confirm`'s styles are now a shared `.prompt` class, used by both dialogs.\n\nThe endpoints are `GET /api/version`, `POST /api/update` (install only) and `POST /api/update/restart`, which refuses when nothing is installed. That way, a page already open on v0.1.7 still reloads after updating to a build with this change.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\nopencode server listening on http://127.0.0.1:4096\n===/tmp/ocspike.port===\n4096\n===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\nMain already has a self-update from #25. This PR keeps what #25 did well and swaps in the stronger parts of this branch.\n\n## What changes compared to main\n\n- **Pure Go install.** `drawa --update` and the page now download the release asset, check it against `checksums.txt`, and swap the binary in atomically (staged next to it, then `rename`). Before, they ran `install.sh` from `main`, so an update depended on whatever `main` held at that moment. It no longer needs `sh`, `curl` or `tar`, and downloads time out after 5 minutes.\n- **Numeric version comparison.** Tags are compared number by number, so `v0.10.0` counts as newer than `v0.9.0`. Covered by tests, along with reading the release tag from the `releases/latest` redirect.\n- **A small update dialog instead of the bottom notice.** It shows `v0.1.6 \u2192 v0.1.7` with a *What's new* link, *Not now*, *Update*, and *Skip this version* as a quiet text link. The app behind it is only lightly dimmed.\n  - *Not now* asks again in a day, and *Skip this version* waits for the next release. It also checks when you return to the tab, so it can't pop up every time you switch back.\n  - **Update installs now, and the restart is your choice.** After installing, the dialog asks *Restart now* or *Restart later*. That's also where it warns that restarting stops sessions that are still working. With *Restart later*, the new version starts the next time you run drawa, and the server remembers the install so the dialog doesn't offer that version again.\n  - Progress and errors show inside the dialog. An error offers *Try again* and points to `drawa --update`.\n  - After *Restart now*, the page reloads once the server answers as the new version.\n- `#confirm`'s styles are now a shared `.prompt` class, used by both dialogs.\n\nThe endpoints are `GET /api/version`, `POST /api/update` (install only) and `POST /api/update/restart`, which refuses when nothing is installed. That way, a page already open on v0.1.7 still reloads after updating to a build with this change.\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.log===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.log 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/ocspike.port===\" && cat /tmp/ocspike.port 2>/dev/null; echo \"===/tmp/pr24.md (first lines)===\" && head -15 /tmp/pr24.md 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1790495285162,"end":1790495285197}},"id":"prt_0e1d5de33001b8jJOeaQv6zSDr","sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","messageID":"msg_0e1d5cfea001rxUdU3ICS59WmO"},"time":1790495285197}}
