{"id":"evt_0e1d5eb60001mhnuKI19g7u59w","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","part":{"id":"prt_0e1d5e451001aWaoIJ5DvfpVZ2","messageID":"msg_0e1d5e0170015G5UsnbVO26OL3","sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","type":"reasoning","text":"So `/tmp` contains a bunch of unrelated scratch work from a session. `ocspike` in `/tmp` is just an empty git repo I was asked to explore. The `/tmp/ocspike.log` and `/tmp/ocspike.port` are related to the opencode server, not the repo.\n\nNow, let me confirm one more time there are no submodules or packed refs with more content.\n\nI have enough. Let me write the summary.\n\nKey finding: The repository is an empty scaffold. There is nothing to summarize in terms of architecture, tests, source, etc. I should report this clearly and honestly rather than fabricating.\n\nLet me do one last check for git objects that might be unreferenced (already did fsck --lost-found which returned nothing). And check .git contents for anything unusual like a `packed-refs` with other branches. Already checked branches - only master. Remotes - none.\n\nLet me verify the .git directory structure just to be complete and make sure there's no worktree/linked git dir pointing elsewhere.","time":{"start":1790495286353,"end":1790495288159}},"time":1790495288160}}
