{"id":"evt_0e1d61688001YFCCDPY0S2hnGR","type":"message.part.updated","properties":{"sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","part":{"id":"prt_0e1d6000d0016S1Z6QQRUBO1sH","messageID":"msg_0e1d5f8b8001M87yAkkcV7FSKn","sessionID":"ses_f1e2a5cdfffeUyUb0fyzH4ONow","type":"text","text":"I've completed a thorough exploration. The findings are conclusive.\n\n## Summary: `/tmp/ocspike` is an empty placeholder repository\n\n**This repository contains no project.** It is a bare-minimum `git init` scaffold with a single placeholder file. There is no source code, no build manifest, no tests, and no architecture to analyze.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Top-level contents of `/tmp/ocspike`\n\n```\ndrwxr-xr-x  .git                  # git metadata (only real directory)\n-rw-r--r--  note.txt              # 12 bytes, 1 line\n```\n\nThat is the *entire* working tree \u2014 verified with `find` (including hidden files) and `git ls-files`. Total size is 120K, almost all of it `.git`.\n\n### 2. What the project is\n\n**It isn't a project yet.** I searched for every common build manifest (`package.json`, `go.mod`, `Cargo.toml`, `pyproject.toml`, `setup.py`, `pom.xml`, `build.gradle`) in the repo and within 3 levels of `/tmp` \u2014 none exist anywhere.\n\n- **Name:** none declared (directory name only)\n- **Purpose:** none declared \u2014 no README, LICENSE, docs, or description\n- **Language:** undetermined\n- **Entry points:** none\n\nThe only content in the whole history is `note.txt`:\n\n```\nhello world\n```\n\n**Git history** \u2014 a single commit, nothing hidden:\n```\n32c0eb8  init\nAuthor: a <a@b>   Date: Sun Sep 27 2026\nnote.txt | 1 +\n```\n\nI confirmed there is no additional content recoverable: only one branch (`master`), no remotes, no tags, no stashes, no packed refs, and `git fsck --lost-found` reports no dangling or unreachable objects. The full object database is three objects (commit, empty tree, one blob).\n\n### 3. Source directory tree\n\nNone. There are no source directories, vendored dependencies, or `node_modules`.\n\n```\n/tmp/ocspike\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .git/          # 2 loose objects, 1 commit, default sample hooks only\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 note.txt       # the sole tracked file: \"hello world\"\n```\n\n### 4. Test setup\n\nNone. No test files, no test runner config, no CI configuration (`.github/`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, etc.), and no way to run tests. The only hooks present are git's unmodified `*.sample` templates, which git never executes.\n\n### 5. Architectural patterns\n\nNone \u2014 there is no code to analyze.\n\n---\n\n### Two incidental observations\n\n- **`.git/opencode`** (not part of git's own format) contains the 40-char SHA `32c0eb8...`, i.e. the current commit. This appears to be a marker written by an OpenCode tooling run, not project content.\n- **A misleading naming coincidence:** `/tmp` also contains `ocspike.log` and `ocspike.port`, but these are *not* related to the repository. They belong to an unrelated `opencode server listening on http://127.0.0.1:4096` process. The other files in `/tmp` (`pr24.md`, `pd.patch`, `chr9333/`) are scratch work about an unrelated Go project called \"drawa\" \u2014 do not mistake any of it for `ocspike` content.\n\n**Bottom line:** if you expected a real codebase at this path, you likely have the wrong directory, or the clone/checkout never ran. I made no modifications to any files.","time":{"start":1790495293453,"end":1790495299208}},"time":1790495299208}}
